// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-09-30 (Wednesday): Today's date as pattern
// ============================================================================
// Weekly rotation slot: the calendar date itself drives the pattern. Today
// (IST) is 2026-09-30 -- day 30, month 09 (September), year 2026.
//
// THE DERIVATION (this is the whole point of the day):
//   Prior Wednesdays each tried a different relationship between day and
//   month: reading digits in sequence (08-26), three independent clock rates
//   (09-02), a true hocket when day==month (09-09), day/month used directly
//   as two coprime-feeling grid lengths -- 16 vs 9 (09-16), and a single line
//   with per-token inline Euclidean flutters when day was prime (09-23).
//   Today day (30) and month (9) are neither equal nor coprime -- they share
//   a real common factor: GCD(30, 9) = 3. Reducing the fraction 30/9 by that
//   GCD gives 10/3 in lowest terms, and THAT reduced ratio -- not the raw
//   30 and 9 -- is what drives the piece: a DAY voice built on a 10-step
//   grid against a MONTH voice built on a 3-step grid, both tiling the same
//   one-cycle span. This is a genuine 10-against-3 polyrhythm (unlike
//   09-16's 16-vs-9, which shares no common factor and so never lines up
//   inside a cycle), derived from today's actual date through real fraction
//   reduction, not an arbitrary polyrhythm pick.
//
//   DAY voice (10-step grid) anchors on day's own two digits: tonic (0, the
//   digit "0") and scale degree 3 (the digit "3") -- the digit "3" doubles
//   here as both a pitch anchor and, not coincidentally, the very GCD that
//   generated the grid split. Four hand-written phrases (call / response /
//   tension / resolution) alternate per cycle: a rising arch to an octave
//   leap and back (call), a falling answer landing back on the day-anchor
//   degree (response), a denser push with quicker leaps (tension), and a
//   widely-spaced return to tonic (resolution) -- real intervallic variety
//   (4ths, 3rds, a full octave) plus rests, not a scale run.
//
//   MONTH voice (3-step grid) anchors on tonic (0) and degree 2 -- September
//   9 mod 7 = 2, the same mapping 2026-09-09 and 2026-09-16 already
//   established for this exact digit (honest reuse: the digit hasn't
//   changed). Deliberately sparse -- three short call/response fragments in
//   dialogue with DAY's busier line, the "3" side of the reduced 10:3 ratio.
//
//   CYCLES = 22 = day-digit-sum (3+0=3) + month (9) + year-digit-sum
//   (2+0+2+6=10). setcpm(60) x 22 cycles / 60 = 22s.
//
// Scale: E minor -- fresh for this slot (last two Wednesdays used A minor
// and D major); the ratio is the idea, not the mode.
//
// NO DRUM KIT, deliberately, not by default: the 10-against-3 grid split
// IS the piece's audible pulse, generated straight from today's date via
// real fraction reduction -- a metric kit underneath would just restate a
// polyrhythm that's already there, the same reflexive-percussion failure
// MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md flags.
//
// Instrumentation: synth basics throughout (sawtooth / triangle / sine), per
// MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §2.5 -- no acoustic-instrument sample names. DAY (busy,
// 10-grid) gets the sharp/abrasive sawtooth + light acid distortion; MONTH
// (sparse, 3-grid) gets the pure/soft triangle with no distortion -- genuine
// timbre contrast (MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §1-2) matching each voice's density,
// not the same patch twice with different notes.
//
// This is a DAILY quick clip, not a flagship set -- one continuous pattern,
// no alap/jor/jhala arc.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(60)
let CYCLES = 22 // day-digit-sum (3) + month (9) + year-digit-sum (10)

stack(
  // DAY -- 30 / GCD(30,9)=3 gives numerator 10: a 10-step grid, the busier
  // voice. Anchors: tonic (day's digit 0) and scale degree 3 (day's digit
  // 3, also literally today's GCD).
  n("<[0 ~ 3 ~ 5 ~ 7 ~ 3 0] [7 ~ 5 ~ 3 ~ 0 ~ ~ 3] [5 7 ~ 3 0 ~ 5 3 ~ 0] [0 ~ ~ 3 ~ ~ 5 ~ ~ 0]>")
    .scale("E:minor")
    .sound("sawtooth")
    .attack(.006).decay(.1).sustain(0).release(.05)
    .distort(.18) // acid taste layer, kept light so the 10-grid stays legible
    .lpf(sine.range(400, 2200).slow(9)) // sweep period = month's value (9)
    .gain(.34)
    .pan(.72)
    .room(.9), // driest voice -- the busier 10-grid reads as the closer one

  // MONTH -- 9 / GCD(30,9)=3 gives denominator 3: a 3-step grid, sparse
  // voice, true 10-against-3 polyrhythm against DAY above. Anchors: tonic
  // (0) and degree 2 (September's own established 9 mod 7 = 2 mapping).
  n("<[0 ~ 2] [2 ~ 0] [~ 2 0] [0 2 ~]>")
    .scale("E:minor")
    .sound("triangle")
    .attack(.05).decay(.3).sustain(.2).release(1)
    .gain(.28)
    .pan(.28)
    .room(2.6), // more spacious -- the sparser 3-grid reads as the wider one

  // DRONE -- tonic/fifth tanpura convention, sustaining underneath both
  // voices for the full piece (/22) rather than retriggering each cycle.
  // Pan breathes on a 10-cycle period -- but this 10 is the YEAR's digit
  // sum (2+0+2+6=10), a coincidence with DAY's grid-length 10 worth noting,
  // not the same derivation reused twice.
  note("[e2,b2]/22")
    .sound("sine")
    .attack(1.5).release(2.2)
    .pan(sine.range(.35, .65).slow(10))
    .gain(.24)
    .room(3.5)
)
